// RUNNER-ISOLATION SECURITY FLOOR — gunbc is PUBLIC on the private self-hosted fleet (srv1/srv2),
// so fork-PR `pull_request` runs execute attacker-controlled code on those runners. The operator
// runner de-privilege (jobs run as the unprivileged `ghrunner` user, not root, no passwordless
// sudo) is the ONLY thing keeping fork-PR code off srv1/srv2 root. That de-priv lives in the
// fleet's actions-runner host config, OUTSIDE this repo — so a silent host-side regression
// (runner re-installed as root, sudoers loosened) would re-expose the fleet with NO in-repo diff
// to catch it. This policy is the in-CI regression guard: a cheap job that adversarially probes
// its OWN runtime privilege on every run and fails closed the moment the runner is re-privileged.
// It is a structural FLOOR, not a component-gated job: it runs unconditionally (no `affected`
// mask, no draft gate) because the fork-PR exposure exists wherever a runner executes at all.
// ci.yml coverage: the `infra_isolation` job + its carrier Job record are bound byte-for-byte by
// the full-workflow carrier dsl/gunbc/ci_github_actions_workflow.dag (structural-match + SHA-pin
// tests in t_ci_workflow_as_data_demo_test) — no dedicated hand-Rust binding test (P5: that carrier
// already deep-covers the projection; a separate assertion would only grow src/v3 hand-Rust).
// The check set is live-verified against the operator de-priv by calm-gull-119 (CI floor
// coordination, 2026-06-01): the de-privileged `ghrunner` account is non-root, member of NONE of
// {docker, sudo, lxd, wheel, root}, cannot read the GitHub App private key at
// /etc/actions-runner/app.pem, has no passwordless sudo, and cannot read /var/run/docker.sock
// (docker.sock is a root-equivalent escape primitive). Each fact is a regression sentinel.
type RunnerIsolationPolicy {
  guard_job_name: String // ci.yml job id that enforces the de-priv floor (operator branch-protection key)
  guard_step_name: String // the assertion step name (ci.dag↔ci.yml binding anchor)
  privileged_groups: List<String> // membership in ANY is a de-priv regression — fail closed
  app_private_key_path: String // the GitHub App key; readable by the runner = regression
  docker_socket_path: String // root-equivalent escape primitive; readable OR writable (socket connect) = regression
  forbid_root_uid: Bool // a job running as uid 0 is a de-priv regression — fail closed
  forbid_passwordless_sudo: Bool // `sudo -n` succeeding is root-equivalent — fail closed
  timeout_minutes: Int // 🟡 gated: formatter-int-refinement — must be ≥1
  blocks_required_path: Bool // a privileged runner blocks the merge (wired into ci.needs, not advisory)
}

data ci_runner_isolation_policy: RunnerIsolationPolicy = {
  guard_job_name: "infra_isolation"
  guard_step_name: "Assert runner is de-privileged (adversarial)"
  privileged_groups: ["docker", "sudo", "lxd", "wheel", "root"]
  app_private_key_path: "/etc/actions-runner/app.pem"
  docker_socket_path: "/var/run/docker.sock"
  forbid_root_uid: true
  forbid_passwordless_sudo: true
  timeout_minutes: 5
  blocks_required_path: true
}

// 🟡 gated — CI build-cache projection NOT YET MODELED HERE — feature:elastic-cache-interface
//   — authority: dsl/std/cache_interface.dag (Modeling DFS Worksheet B; landed PR #4095). The
//   internal planning worksheets (elastic-cache-interface / elastic-ci-redesign) were deleted in
//   #4192 for the public-repo flip, so the in-repo substrate file + that PR are the durable refs.
//   The backend substrate already landed in dsl/std/cache_interface.dag as first-authority
//   `CacheInterfaceFacts` rows: `sccache_local_facts` (PerHostFilesystem),
//   `cargo_target_dir_facts` (PerRunnerFilesystem), `gha_actions_cache_facts`,
//   `buildbuddy_cas_facts`, `rustup_toolchain_store_facts`. The MISSING piece is this file's
//   consumer (cache_interface.dag line 20: "consumer: ci harness cache projection"): nothing in
//   src/v4/workflow/*.dag imports cache_interface yet, so the ci_floor cache transport is still
//   hand-authored `actions/cache` blocks in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
//   dissolve-on-arrival: when this projection lands, the ci_floor `Cache Cargo` / `Cache gunbc
//   binary` steps in ci.yml are projected from cache_key_projection over these facts (identity =
//   content_hash(canonical Upsert<T> subject), NOT hashFiles), and the interim hand blocks below
//   are deleted. forbidden (per the cache_interface.dag identity discipline): hand-authored cache
//   keys at any layer (`hashFiles(...)`, `cache_key:` strings, sccache `--cache-mode-key`) as the
//   standing design, and stacking sccache/`RUSTC_WRAPPER` into ci.yml ahead of `CacheInterfaceFacts`
//   projection (the "immediate local patch" the worksheet named as a P2 violation).
//   INTERIM (operator 2026-06-01, "stop the bleeding"): the ci.yml `Cache Cargo` key was
//   de-churned (Cargo.lock+toolchain only) so restores actually hit and stop evicting the warm
//   v2 `gunbc-bin` cache. This is transport repair of an existing block, not new design surface,
//   and does NOT touch the two dominant ci_floor steps (M1 emit-probe v2 compile, v2→v4
//   bootstrap ~9m) — those compile freshly-emitted trees in $RUNNER_TEMP whose target/ is
//   discarded each run, so only content-addressed sccache (the modeled projection) can warm them.

